# DBRepair-Windows

Release notes for the Windows counterpart to DBRepair.sh (DBRepair-Windows.ps1)

# Release Info

v1.02.00
  - PMS 1.43+ / SQLite 3.44+: `PRAGMA integrity_check` now also validates FTS3/FTS4 content and reports
    "malformed inverted index for FTS4 table ..." on databases which SQLite 3.39.4 called `ok`.
    That is FTS index drift, not database corruption, so the integrity check no longer fails the run when
    every finding is an inverted-index line - it logs a warning and continues.
  - Add an FTS index rebuild to automatic maintenance.  After REINDEX (and before the new databases are
    made active), every FTS4 virtual table is rebuilt with `INSERT INTO <t>(<t>) VALUES('rebuild')` and
    then verified with `('integrity-check')`.  Only a failing integrity-check fails the run.
    (A dump/reload copies the FTS shadow tables verbatim, so the indexes must be rebuilt explicitly.)

v1.01.02
  - Remove `statistics_bandwidth` pruning, as it's now part of PMS 1.41.8
  - Change `quit` to 98 and `exit` to 99
  - Minor logging refactoring

v1.01.01
  - Add `staticstics_bandwidth` pruning during automatic repair.

v1.01.00
